38 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (As we move into the second half of the year, there is much to be grateful for in our parish community. Our parish fundraising campaign continues to make wonderful progress, with $122,345 raised so far. We now need just $22,655 to reach our goal of $145,000. Thank you to everyone who has contributed so generously. If you have been considering purchasing an engraved paver, please note that the final order will be placed at the end of August. Be sure to submit your order before then so you don't miss out.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
39 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (We are also pleased to advise that the long-awaited structural repairs to our church are expected to commence during August/September. While every effort will be made to minimise disruption, please keep an eye on the weekly parish bulletin for any changes to Mass arrangements while the works are underway.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
40 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (During July, important works were completed in the sacristy and confessional. These improvements ensure our parish remains compliant with the Archdiocese's safeguarding requirements, helping us provide a safe and welcoming environment for all.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
41 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (On 25 July, we were delighted to welcome members of the Sullivan family as they celebrated the centenary of their family's arrival in Australia. It was a wonderful occasion, and we thank them for sharing this special milestone with our parish community.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
42 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (Looking ahead, we warmly invite everyone to join us on Saturday, 22 August, when the St Thomas Year 4 students will celebrate Mass with our parish, followed by a sausage sizzle. It promises to be a lovely opportunity for fellowship and to support our young people as they continue to grow in faith.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
43 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (Finally, a gentle reminder that Holy Hour is held every Friday. In the busyness of daily life, spending an hour in quiet prayer before the Blessed Sacrament is a beautiful opportunity to deepen our relationship with God. Whether you can stay for the whole hour or just a few moments, all are welcome.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
